---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import RatingBadge from '../../components/RatingBadge.astro';
import { destinations, destMonthUrl, deg, MONTHS } from '../../lib/data';

// European beach destinations with sea-temperature data.
const pool = destinations.filter((d) => d.region === 'Europe' && d.tags.includes('beach') && d.months.every((m) => m.sea !== null));
// Rank by the weather score (warmer sea breaks ties); only list places where the sea is at least 18°C.
const byMonth = MONTHS.map((_, m) =>
  [...pool]
    .filter((d) => d.months[m].sea! >= 18)
    .sort((a, b) => b.months[m].score - a.months[m].score || b.months[m].sea! - a.months[m].sea!)
    .slice(0, 5),
);
---

<Guide slug="best-beaches-europe-by-month" photo="sardinia">
  <p>
    Europe's beach season runs from about <strong>June to October</strong> around the Mediterranean, when the sea is warm and
    the sun reliable. In spring and autumn the best bets are in the south and east — Cyprus, Crete, southern Spain and the
    Algarve — and in winter only the <strong>Canary Islands</strong> and <strong>Madeira</strong> are warm enough for the beach.
    We ranked {pool.length} European beach destinations for every month by weather, and show the average sea temperature, so
    you know whether it's a swimming or a sunbathing trip.
  </p>

  {
    byMonth.map((items, m) => (
      <>
        <h2>Best beaches in Europe in {MONTHS[m]}</h2>
        {items.length ? (
          <ul class="picks">
            {items.map((d) => (
              <li>
                <a href={destMonthUrl(d, m)}>{d.name}</a> <RatingBadge score={d.months[m].score} rating={d.months[m].rating} note={d.months[m].note} />
                <span class="muted small">air {deg(d.months[m].high)} · sea {deg(d.months[m].sea!)}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        ) : (
          <p class="muted">Nowhere in Europe has a sea of 18°C or more in {MONTHS[m]}.</p>
        )}
      </>
    ))
  }

  <h2>Sea temperatures and swimming</h2>
  <p>
    Around 18°C feels bracing, 22°C is comfortable for a long swim and 25°C or more feels warm. The Mediterranean is warmest in
    August and September; the Atlantic coasts of Portugal and the Canaries stay cooler but more even through the year. See{' '}
    <a href="/guides/mediterranean-sea-temperatures/">Mediterranean sea temperatures by month</a> for the full table.
  </p>
  <p class="small muted">Sea temperatures are 2023–2025 averages from the Open-Meteo Marine API; ratings combine air temperature and rainfall.</p>

  <h2>Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Go in June or September</b> for warm seas without the August crowds and prices.</li>
    <li><b>Book early for August</b>, when much of Europe takes its holidays and coastal towns fill up.</li>
    <li>See also <a href="/best-time-to-visit-mediterranean/">the best time to visit the Mediterranean</a>, <a href="/best-time-to-visit-greek-islands/">the Greek islands</a> and <a href="/best-time-to-visit-canary-islands/">the Canary Islands</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</Guide>

<style>
  .picks {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .picks li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }
</style>
